course: dictionary
lesson: 15646
title: Theatrical
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Theatrical has two main meanings, and both connect to the theatre. First, it means about plays and acting: «The theatrical company rehearsed all week for the show.» The clues are company, rehearsed and show, which all belong to putting on a play.
explain: Second, theatrical means showy and exaggerated, as if someone is acting for an audience. «She gave a theatrical sigh and flopped onto the sofa.» Nobody was really that tired. The sigh was made big so that people would notice. Ask yourself: is this person doing something real, or putting on a show?
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «She gave a showy sigh and flopped onto the sofa» still makes sense, so showy is a good match. The context tells you which meaning the author means.
fact: Theatrical means about the theatre, plays and acting.
fact: Theatrical also means exaggerated and showy, as if acting for an audience.
fact: «Don't be so theatrical!» means don't make such a big show of your feelings.
fact: Theatricals are plays put on by ordinary people, not professional actors.
fact: In drama lessons, theatrical often goes with stage, costumes, lighting and props.
exercise: What does theatrical mean in «theatrical costumes»? | *About plays and acting, made for the stage | Quiet and hidden away | Written down in a book | Very cold and wet
exercise: «He gave a theatrical gasp when he saw the cake.» What does theatrical suggest? | Hungry and tired | *Big and showy, as if performing for others | Sad and lonely | Calm and quiet
exercise: What are amateur theatricals? | Large family dinners | *Plays put on by ordinary people, not professional actors | Costumes sold in shops | Lessons about maths and science
test: Which word could replace theatrical in «She made a theatrical entrance through the door»? | *Showy | Tiny | Quiet | Muddy
test: What do drama lessons often use that is theatrical? | Muddy football boots | Sums and spelling tests | *Costumes and props for a play | Weather charts
exam: Mum says, «Don't be so theatrical!» when I scream about a tiny spider. What does theatrical mean here? | Costumed for a party | Acting in a real play on a stage | Quiet and shy | *Making a big show of your feelings, as if performing for others
